1. Cut the canon recaps. Every speaker retells their own missions to people who were there. Jack even says "you all know the Purgatory version." This is the main thing that makes the script hard to read, and it pushes Thomas offstage for pages at a time. A good rule: keep a canon event only at the moment Thomas walks into it. Tali already does this to herself ("I've just given you a status report"), so use her as the model. Passages to cut or shrink:
Jack: Purgatory, Pragia, the Collector base play-by-play, the Grissom battle
Joker: the clone plot
Liara: Vendetta and Javik, Hagalaz, most of Thessia
Grunt: the Rite, Utukku
James: Omega, Vancouver
Kaidan: Brain Camp, Horizon, Mars. Keep the Spectre argument and the coup; that's the best payoff in the script.
Wrex: the genophage summary
EDI: Cronos Station

2. Stop outing him. The sheet says Joker never brings up the hospitals unless Thomas does. Several speakers say they won't tell something and then tell it.
Let Jack be the one who breaks the silence, about the hands, on purpose. Everyone else should visibly hold back.
Joker keeps the hospital ratings but stops himself: "I'd say, buddy, you—" and then he swallows it. That's more Joker, and it hits harder.
The mother story belongs to Liara only. Jack currently retells it.

3. Give each trait to one speaker.
"Cooking came second" appears four times (Jack, Joker, Grunt, Wrex). Keep it with Jack.
"He outdrank everyone" appears three times. Keep it with Joker.
"He gave the win away" comes from almost everyone. Keep Joker's ratings and Tali's locker count.
"The body's going to Rouen, Wrex told me" is told three times. Keep it with Wrex.

4. Save Jack's collapse for the end. Her first turn already has the full "come back… please…" breakdown, so the recording scene repeats a beat we've already seen. In turn one, let her nearly break and swallow it; "Give me a second" is enough. In consequence, she can say less at the start, the more the final turn costs her.

5. Give him flaws, and show the snap once. Right now he reads as a saint with a tremor. The sheet's Thomas runs when someone gets close, chases when they pull away, and soothes others before asking for anything himself. Two additions would fix this:
Each flaw should cost someone in the room something, and that person should be the one who says it. Here are beats you could drop in, each tied to a pattern from the sheet:
Chases when she pulls back (Jack)
During a bad week at Grissom her voice notes got shorter, and his messages got longer. "Three messages apologizing for the one before. Then one apologizing for the apologies. I sent back: I'm not leaving, I'm busy, a kid set a desk on fire. He wrote 'okay.' Then three pages."
White-knighting (Jack)
"He went to Sanders behind my back and asked if I was sleeping. I nearly put him through the hull. He didn't argue. Said, you're right, I do that, I'll stop. And he did. Mostly."
His needs arrive late (Tali)
"His bench mount failed for three weeks before I found out. He'd been redoing every joint twice at night rather than ask me to look at it. He said I was busy with the geth. I was. I'd have stopped."
Can't be cared for (Joker)
"I brought him a sandwich once. No reason, I just did. I'm a pilot, it was a terrible sandwich. He was so embarrassed to need help, he got up and made me a better one. I could've killed him." (No reason given on purpose: Joker doesn't say why Thomas was in bed. Point 2 wins.)
Intellectualizing (Liara)
"He could describe his own wound like a paper he'd peer-reviewed, citations and all. I asked him once how it truly felt. He said he never knew, laughed, and went to make tea. He never came back with the answer."
Leaves first (Liara)
"He told me he'd left a woman on Earth before she could leave him, and called it kindness. I said it was the opposite. He agreed far too quickly, which is how I knew he'd do it again."
Humor as a wall (Kaidan)
"Every time I got near Akuze, there was a joke. A good one. I laughed every time, and it took me a year to see that was the point."
Drinking to cope (Kaidan)
This turns "he outdrank everyone" from a brag into something true. "Everybody tells that as a party story. I'm not going to tell mine. I'll just say I was up at six some nights too, and he wasn't at a party." (Kaidan holds back, per point 2. He hints and doesn't say it.)
The snap, and the guilt after (James)
A Terra Firma type at a bar tells a turian waitress humanity should have finished the job at Shanxi. Thomas gives him one quiet warning ("Don't say that again. I'm giving you a chance."), and the guy says it again. This is the only kind of thing he'd ever throw a punch over, and he can't fight, so the punch is clumsy on purpose. "Worst punch I ever saw. Thumb inside the fist. Guy went down mostly from surprise. After, Thomas sat on the curb with ice on his hand, shaking worse than ever, and said, 'I'm bad even at this.'"
Lifts that overpromise (EDI)
"One week he committed to eleven tasks in thirty hours. He finished four. Then he slept, and apologized to seven people one by one. None of them had noticed. He had."
Bad memory (Grunt)
"He forgot my decanting day. Three weeks late, a crate came to Tuchanka. A plastic Earth lizard, a dinosaur, with a note: 'Late. Sorry. It looked like you.' I didn't know I had a decanting day until he forgot it. It's on my armour rack."
Two principles to keep in mind:
Not every flaw gets fixed. Leave at least one unresolved. Jack never got him to take the classroom, and that should hurt more than any flaw he grew out of.
Write flaws as things he did, not as diagnoses. "He forgot my decanting day" lands harder than "his memory was bad," and it lets the speaker's love show in how they tell it.


The crew abduction: in ME2 the crew is taken before the relay jump. So there's no ship full of people saying goodbye, and Thomas is missing from Jack's list of people pulled from the pods. Fix: he hid in the ducts with Joker. That's a great story for Joker's turn. (Dropped the pod option. It would mean he wasn't aboard the night before, which kills "Don't make it weird" and the stove "I love you".)
Also: the "whole ship saying goodbye" in Jack's Omega-4 passage becomes the squad, Joker and EDI. thomas.notes.md "Escalation" has been fixed the same way.
Wrex's first-day plate: Wrex was only aboard the SR-1, before Thomas cooked, and Mordin wasn't there. Move the scene to the Citadel shore leave (two days off). Knock-on changes: Mordin is dead by then, so the "old salarian at the med-bay door" line goes or someone else takes it. Wrex's ryncol "second week" behind the flour becomes the first night. Grunt's "Wrex, you tried twice" now fits the shore leave.
EDI's first meeting: on the SR-2 she was openly introduced as an AI, so "worked out what I was" doesn't fit. Try "the first to ask me something that wasn't an order.”

Voice and line level
Jack's Britishisms: she's American, but "arse," "you lot," "taking the piss," "colour" and "organising" read British.
Jack's "sweetheart" to Liara isn't her.
The mosh-pit aside breaks the quietest moment of her first turn.
French-English slips: "an hardcore," "at any occasion," and a space before "?".



The strongest bonds come from mirrored wounds, where each character recognizes their own thing in him. Here are parallels for each one, with a sample line:
Tali: a parent taken by something else. Rael loved her and chose his work; Thomas's mother loved him and was taken by grief and drink. Both stood trial for a parent, in a way. "At my trial, he was the only one who didn't tell me my father loved me. He said, 'Loving you and choosing you aren't the same thing.' Then he asked what I wanted to build first, on a planet we didn't have yet."
Joker: family left behind. Joker's family was on Tiptree when the Reapers hit, and Thomas's was in Rouen. They could have waited for news together. "We had a deal. Whoever heard first said nothing until the other one heard too. We sat in that cockpit for three days, not saying anything, for once."
Liara: the parent who stays. When she learned her father was a bartender on Illium, Thomas, whose father was the quiet steady one, but obsessed by his work, could have pushed her to go. "He was the only one who didn't laugh. He said his own father never left and was never quite there either, always inside his work, and that a father pouring drinks across the station was the same distance, only easier to cross. 'Go sit at her bar. A counter is a short distance.' I did. Twice."
Grunt: made for other people. Okeer designed Grunt, and Thomas built himself to fit everyone else. Both are afraid they're fake. "I asked him if I was real or just Okeer's idea. He said he'd asked himself the same thing. I said, 'Okeer made me. You made you, for everyone else. Same tank.' He didn't joke for a whole minute."
James: feeling undeserving. James was offered N7 and didn't think he'd earned it. "He started telling me all the things that made me the best person for the position. Then I asked if that went for him too, for his position, and he changed the subject to eggs."
Kaidan: bodies that betray them. Kaidan has migraines from his implant, Thomas has the tremor, and both live with medication. "We compared pill cases once. His had more compartments. He said that made him the senior officer."
Wrex: rejected by a parent. Wrex's father tried to kill him; Thomas's mother told him he wasn't hers. "We compared. I said mine was worse. He didn't argue, and he didn't agree. He poured. Mine was worse."
Wrex is also about to become a father, while Thomas was half a father to his youngest sister, and started to want one. (Wrex speaking.) "I asked him what you do with a small one. He said, 'Mostly you show up.' I asked when he was having one. He said when he was good enough. I told him that's not how it works. Nobody's good enough. You show up."
Three devices could tie all of this together:
What each person gave him. Right now the script is almost all about what he gave others. Have each speaker name one thing they gave back, and whether he managed to accept it. His trouble receiving care then shows up across the whole room instead of being described once.
A playlist for each of them. He made everyone one, and what's on it shows what he saw in them. It also gives EDI a reason to have the files :



His habits, now theirs. Grunt chops in a straight line, Joker says "you win" to someone, Kaidan passes the hot sauce without the joke, Jack learns to care for people. Some speakers catch themselves doing something of his, which shows him living on in them without anyone having to say so.


Playlists :
"Thane: Imperfect Meomries" :Post rock, ambient black metal, religious chants
"Kaidan: Can I help?": Country, Varieté, love song
"Tali: Bosh'tet. All of them" Pitchfork coded. Oriental twists for quarian wanderlust and drum'n'bass to hack geth.
"Jack: Rough stuff, I like it." Hardcore, techno and hyperpop
"Joker: Funny Robot-fucker" Alt-rock, goofy tunes, Weezers
"Liara: Information Archeologist" Jazz, classical, sad/emo stuff and hacker music + a touch of bad bitch rap
"Miranda: The perfect B": Opera, doll pop
"Traynor: Toothbrush operator" Rap, pop
"James: 184": Funk, happy music, top workout songs, random stuffs
"Grunt: Krantt Krew": Skate punk, nu-metal, dubstep
"Wrex: If I die, I'll kill him.": Heavy beatdown, war chants, harsh noise




Added from review (2026-10-15)

More outing to remove (point 2):
Joker: "Third time in a hospital", and "what happened when he tried to end his life". He keeps the whole log and says he has it, not what's in it.
EDI: the three admission years read out with their context, and "hypomanic, type two". She visibly declines to read the file.
Jack, last turn: "years of wanting to be dead" and the "his hospitals, my labs" mother retelling. The mother story is Liara's.

More repeats (point 3):
The Akuze/Shepard origin is told five times (Tali, Joker, James, Kaidan, Jack). Jack's last turn keeps it. The others reference Shepard without retelling it.
Kropotkin by name is said five times. Liara keeps it.
"He joked about his hands first" is said four times (Jack, Tali, James, EDI). Jack keeps it.
ABBA comes up four times. Jack's music passage keeps it. Elsewhere, use the playlists.
Jack's first turn ("Wrex got told he was wrong") gives away Wrex's turn before he speaks.

More recaps to shrink (point 1): Joker's SR-1 crash, James's Fehl Prime, EDI's London/beam.

More Britishisms (Jack): maths, honour, apologising, favourite, proper, round. Tali's "apologised" too. Spelling is American throughout.
Line slips: "varrens" should be "varren". Liara's "specific different" and her contractions.

Body to Rouen: Wrex owns the telling. Jack's last-turn payoff stays (he never looked at bodies; touch his hair), but without "Wrex told me".
